# Repository overview

This repo has two primary projects plus root-level domain references:

1. `gtp-telemetry/` - a browser-only React/Vite app that parses local `.ibt` files, analyzes them client-side, and renders a dashboard plus PDF export
2. `iracing-gtp-engineer-plugin/` - a plugin/skill package with command docs and a standalone Python IBT parser
3. Root references - `SKILL.md`, `per-car-quirks.md`, `telemetry-channels.md`, and `ibt-parsing-guide.md`

## App architecture

- `gtp-telemetry/src/store/session-store.ts` owns the file -> validate -> parse -> analyze pipeline
- `gtp-telemetry/src/lib/ibt-parser.ts` is the browser parser
- `gtp-telemetry/src/lib/analysis-engine.ts` feeds most dashboard and export views
- `gtp-telemetry/src/components/dashboard/` contains chart and analysis panels

## Plugin architecture

- `iracing-gtp-engineer-plugin/plugin.json` is the manifest
- `iracing-gtp-engineer-plugin/commands/` contains slash command docs
- `iracing-gtp-engineer-plugin/skills/iracing-gtp-engineer/` is the installed skill source
- `iracing-gtp-engineer-plugin/scripts/parse_ibt.py` is the standalone Python parser
- `iracing-gtp-engineer-plugin/install.ps1` must stay in sync with manifest or layout changes

## Expectations

- Keep committed config rooted at repository level unless a subproject is intentionally opened standalone
- Prefer repo-relative guidance over machine-specific assumptions
- Treat parser and telemetry semantics as high-risk areas and make conservative changes
